{"book":{"id":"book-the-slave-power-the-free-north-and-southern-domination-1780-1860-leonard-l-richards","slug":"the-slave-power-the-free-north-and-southern-domination-1780-1860-leonard-l-richards","title":"The Slave Power: The Free North and Southern Domination, 1780–1860","authors":[{"id":"person-leonard-l-richards","name":"Leonard L. Richards"}],"isbn13":["9780807126004"],"subjects":["Race & Ethnicity"],"topics":["Science & Discovery","Slavery & Emancipation","Courts & Trials","Democracy & Elections"],"centralFigures":[],"links":{"amazon":"https://www.amazon.com/s?k=The%20Slave%20Power%3A%20The%20Free%20North%20and%20Southern%20Domination%2C%201780%E2%80%931860%20Leonard%20L.%20Richards","bookshop":"https://bookshop.org/search?keywords=The%20Slave%20Power%3A%20The%20Free%20North%20and%20Southern%20Domination%2C%201780%E2%80%931860%20Leonard%20L.%20Richards","indiebound":"https://www.indiebound.org/search/book?keys=The%20Slave%20Power%3A%20The%20Free%20North%20and%20Southern%20Domination%2C%201780%E2%80%931860%20Leonard%20L.%20Richards","worldcat":"https://search.worldcat.org/search?q=The%20Slave%20Power%3A%20The%20Free%20North%20and%20Southern%20Domination%2C%201780%E2%80%931860%20Leonard%20L.%20Richards","publisher":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL18288659W"},"sourceIds":["source-award-record-lincoln-prize-civil-war-era-gettysburg-college-previous-winners-of-the-gilder-lehrman-lincoln-pr","source-open-library-the-slave-power-the-free-north-and-southern-domination-1780-1860-leonard-l-richards","source-open-library-summary-the-slave-power-the-free-north-and-southern-domination-1780-1860-leonard-l-richards"],"publicationYear":2000,"thumbnailUrl":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/1526485-L.jpg","readerProfile":{"readerLevel":"crossover","narrativeScore":0,"accessibilityScore":0,"scholarlyScore":0,"traits":[],"method":"deterministic_catalog_heuristics_v1"},"renownProfile":{"knowsBook":true,"publicFame":35,"criticalRenown":72,"controversy":28,"llmAffinity":72,"affinityResidual":-3.81,"confidence":{"publicFame":0.86,"criticalRenown":0.84,"controversy":0.75,"llmAffinity":0.94},"tags":{"craft":"craft-of-explanation","evidence":"archival-research","stance":"revisionism"},"model":"gpt-5.6-luna","promptVersion":1},"summary":"\"With The Slave Power, Richards reopens a discussion effectively closed by historians since the 1920s - when the Slave Power theory was dismissed first as a distortion of reality and later as a manifestation of the \"paranoid style\" in the early Republic - and attempts to understand why such reputable leaders accepted this thesis wholeheartedly as truth and why hundreds of thousands of voters responded to their call to arms.\". \"Through incisive biographical cameos and narrative vignettes, Richards explains the evolution of the Slave Power argument over time, tracing the oft-repeated scenario of northern outcry against the perceived slaveocracy, followed by still another \"victory\" for the South: the three-fifths rule in congressional representation; admission of Missouri as a slave state in 1820; the Indian removal of 1830; annexation of Texas in 1845; the Wilmot Proviso of 1847; the Fugitive Slave Law of 1850, and more. Richards probes inter- and intra-party strategies of the Democrats, Free-Soilers, Whigs, and Republicans and revisits national debates over sectional conflicts to elucidate just how the southern Democratic slaveholders - with the help of some northerners - assumed, protected, and eventually lost a dominance that extended from the White House to the Speaker's chair to the Supreme Court.\".","subjectCategories":[{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Politics and government","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-the-slave-power-the-free-north-and-southern-domination-1780-1860-leonard-l-richards"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Extension to the territories","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-the-slave-power-the-free-north-a